+# The Daily Grind
+
+Static homepage with a responsive SMS code verification demo. Open `index.html` in a static host. No build is required.
+
+## Verification
+
+The demo accepts `123456`, expires challenges after five minutes, limits each challenge to five incorrect attempts, and applies a 30-second resend cooldown. It does not send SMS, establish a session, or authenticate a customer. Rewards and online-order links retain the selected destination through the demo.
+
+The form uses one labelled input with `autocomplete="one-time-code"`, `inputmode="numeric"`, full-code paste support, inline errors, keyboard focus management, and live status announcements. Supported browsers can extract a code with the WebOTP API after the customer grants permission. Other browsers retain manual input and operating-system code suggestions.
+
+## Production connection
+
+Replace the demo challenge and comparison in `verification.js` with server endpoints that issue, resend, and verify challenges. Never ship a real code in the client. The server must enforce expiry, attempt limits, resend limits, and challenge-to-phone binding, then establish a secure session before redirecting to Rewards or ordering. The client timers are presentation only.
+
+Start the WebOTP listener **before** requesting SMS delivery. Serve over HTTPS and end the SMS with the host and code, for example:
+
+```text
+Your Daily Grind verification code is 123456.
+
+@your-domain.example #123456
+```
+
+Use the actual host without a scheme, path, or port. Browser support varies, and dismissal or timeout must leave manual entry available. See the [Chrome WebOTP documentation](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/identity/web-apis/web-otp).
+
+## Validation
+
+Run `node --check verification.js` for JavaScript syntax validation. There is no build script or backend in this repository. Existing menu, café, and other destination routes need their respective pages supplied by the hosting application.
